\newlabel{fig:laco}{{4.10}{35}{BSP, C++ backend, exploratory comparison of the constraint reformulation: grounding time (left) and propositional rules (right). \texttt {gc}, \texttt {la}, and \texttt {lc} overlap because they share the quadratic base encoding (some $52.8$ million rules and one to three minutes of grounding at $n=120$); \texttt {la\_co} lies on the horizontal axis of both plots ($366$ rules, milliseconds of grounding), the visual form of the five-orders-of-magnitude gap discussed in the text}{figure.4.10}{}}
